From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowerFS Team
Date: Mon, 11 Aug 2026 08:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fs/xattr: export simple_xattr_* symbols for loadable modules

The simple_xattr API (simple_xattr_get, simple_xattr_set, simple_xattr_list,
simple_xattr_free, simple_xattr_alloc, simple_xattr_add, simple_xattr_space,
simple_xattrs_init, simple_xattrs_free) is used by in-tree filesystems like
tmpfs/shmem, but none of these functions are exported with EXPORT_SYMBOL.

This prevents out-of-tree filesystem modules (such as powerfs.ko) from using
the simple_xattr API for in-memory extended attribute storage.

Export all simple_xattr_* functions with EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL so that loadable
modules can use them.

This patch is required for the PowerFS kernel module's xattr support
(powerfs_fs.c uses xattr_handler + simple_xattr for user/trusted/security
xattr namespaces).

Apply with:
  cd linux-6.17
  patch -p1 < ../kernel/patches/export-simple-xattr-symbols-linux-6.17.patch

Signed-off-by: PowerFS Team
---
 fs/xattr.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/xattr.c b/fs/xattr.c
index abcdef123456..abcdef123457 100644
--- a/fs/xattr.c
+++ b/fs/xattr.c
@@ -1578,6 +1578,15 @@ void simple_xattrs_free(struct simple_xattrs *xattrs, size_t *freed_space)
 		rbp = rbp_next;
 	}
 }
+
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattr_space);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattr_free);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattr_alloc);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattr_get);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattr_set);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattr_list);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattr_add);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattrs_init);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(simple_xattrs_free);
